  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 309 AM EDT Tue Aug 11 2026\n\nBy Thursday and the start of the long term period, mid-level ridging \nwill have situated itself over southern CONUS, with north and \ncentral Georgia positioned on the eastern periphery of the dome of \nhigh pressure. The sensible impacts will be dual-pronged: first, \nincreasingly more oppressive heat through the weekend as the ridge \nstagnates; second, intrusion of moisture and passing disturbances \nrounding the edge of the ridge will support isolated to scattered \nconvection each afternoon. \n\nAfternoon highs will be in the 90s for all but the terrain of \nnortheast Georgia, and it is possible that portions of our far \nsouthern and eastern zones may approach a 100 degree air temperature \nby late week (!). As such, heat index values will surge well into \nthe triple digits. Heat Advisory criteria is likely to be met for at \nleast subsets of the southern and eastern portions of the area, and \nconditions will need to be monitored for potential Extreme Heat \nproducts assuming trends continue. Would not be surprised to see \nforecast dewpoints come down as this heat event enters the purview \nof the short term (perhaps appreciably) -- as afternoon mixing is \ntypically strong under mature ridging -- which would help temper \nsome of the more \"extreme\" heat index values in the forecast. Either \nway, some of the hottest days of the year thus far appear to be in \nour near future -- make next weekend's plans with a high likelihood \nof impactful heat in mind. \n\nA caveat/question mark for the extent of potentially dangerous heat \nlies in our continued afternoon storm chances. Should convection win \nout over building subsidence and materialize, it would serve to \npunctuate/truncate the full breadth of diurnal heating. Dirty ridge \nsetups are not uncommon in the summer, and some quasi-organization \nof storms is possible depending on the strength of features \ntraversing upper flow. Will continue to monitor and carry 20-30% \nPoPs each day for now.",
